<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William Longsword</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 893–942</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William Longsword was the son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rollo">Rollo</a> and ruler of Normandy from about 927 to 942. In 933 King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rudolph-of-france">Rudolph of West Francia</a> granted him further lands in the west, probably the Cotentin and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avranchin">Avranchin</a>, giving Normandy roughly its later borders. He was murdered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/picquigny">Picquigny</a> in 942 by men of Arnulf I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/flanders">Flanders</a>, leaving his young son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a> as heir.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-longsword.jpg" alt="William Longsword" width="320" height="286" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: AnonymousUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:WilliamLongsword.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
